artifact.self_contained_problem:
Let X be a smooth complex projective variety. A vector bundle E on X is called asymptotically generically generated if, for all sufficiently large m, the evaluation map H^0(X, Sym^m E) ⊗ O_X → Sym^m E is surjective on a non-empty Zariski-open subset of X. For such an E, define the Kodaira-type rational map φ_m : X ⇢ Grass(rk Sym^m E - h^0(Sym^m E), Sym^m E*) (or, equivalently, the rational map to projective space induced by sections of Sym^m E on the projectivization P(E)), and define the Iitaka dimension κ(E) of E as the maximum, over m ≫ 0, of the dimension of the image of the associated stabilized Kodaira map; equivalently, κ(E) := κ(O_{P(E)}(1)) when this tautological line bundle is asymptotically generically generated.

Fix numerical invariants — for instance, a rank r ≥ 1 and Chern classes c_1, c_2, … — such that there exists a (coarse) moduli space M = M_X(r; c_1, c_2, …) of Gieseker-semistable vector bundles on X with these invariants. Let M^s ⊂ M denote the open subset parametrizing stable bundles, and assume that every E ∈ M^s for which κ(E) is defined is asymptotically generically generated.

For each integer k ∈ {0, 1, …, dim X + r - 1}, set
   M^s_k := { [E] ∈ M^s : E is asymptotically generically generated and κ(E) = k }.

Investigate the geometric properties of the resulting stratification {M^s_k}_k of M^s. In particular, describe:
(a) which strata are non-empty, and the dimension of each non-empty stratum;
(b) whether each M^s_k is locally closed, constructible, or has a natural scheme structure, and what the closure relations among the strata are;
(c) the behaviour of κ in families, e.g. its semicontinuity properties on M^s;
(d) the geometry (irreducibility, smoothness, singularities) of the strata and of their closures.

